From: LuneOS port <webos-ports@webos-ports.org>
Subject: [PATCH] compasschain: link the magcalibrationchain it calls into

CompassChain::resetCalibration() forwards to MagCalibrationChain, but the
plugin only added magcalibrationchain to INCLUDEPATH and never linked it. The
library builds regardless, carrying an undefined
_ZN19MagCalibrationChain16resetCalibrationEv with no DT_NEEDED that could
resolve it, and sensorfwd then rejects it at load:

  Plugin loading error: "compasschain" - "Cannot load library
  /usr/lib/sensord-qt6/libcompasschain-qt6.so: undefined symbol:
  _ZN19MagCalibrationChain16resetCalibrationEv"
  plugin marked invalid: "compasschain" / "compasssensor"

compasssensor is invalidated along with it, and sensortestapp aborts outright
with the shipped testapp.conf because loading that plugin fails.

Link it the same way every other component here links a sibling library, and
declare the build dependency that link implies. chains/ is not CONFIG+=ordered
- only the top-level .pro is, and that only serialises chains against filters,
sensors, ... not the subdirs inside chains/ - so without compasschain.depends
make starts both subdirs at once and the link races the library it needs:

  ld: cannot find -lmagcalibrationchain-qt6

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/chains/compasschain/compasschain.pro	2026-08-30 09:12:49.417446080 +0200
+++ b/chains/compasschain/compasschain.pro	2026-08-30 09:12:49.430621926 +0200
@@ -17,4 +17,14 @@
                ../../filters/magcoordinatealignfilter \
                ../../filters/declinationfilter
 
+# CompassChain::resetCalibration() calls through to MagCalibrationChain, so the
+# plugin has to link the chain that defines it. Without this the .so builds but
+# carries an undefined _ZN19MagCalibrationChain16resetCalibrationEv and no
+# DT_NEEDED for it, and sensorfwd rejects the plugin at load:
+#   Plugin loading error: "compasschain" - "Cannot load library
+#   libcompasschain-qt6.so: undefined symbol: ..."
+# which invalidates compasssensor too, and makes sensortestapp abort with the
+# stock testapp.conf.
+LIBS += -L../magcalibrationchain -lmagcalibrationchain-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}
+
 include( ../chain-config.pri )
--- a/chains/chains.pro	2026-09-03 10:01:13.366234061 +0200
+++ b/chains/chains.pro	2026-09-03 10:01:13.372234167 +0200
@@ -7,3 +7,12 @@
            orientationchain \
            magcalibrationchain \
            compasschain
+
+# compasschain links -lmagcalibrationchain-qt$${QT_MAJOR_VERSION}, so it cannot
+# be built at the same time as the chain it links. This directory is not
+# CONFIG+=ordered (only the top level is, and that only serialises chains
+# against filters, sensors, ... - not the subdirs within it), so without an
+# explicit dependency make is free to start both at once and compasschain's
+# link step loses the race:
+#   ld: cannot find -lmagcalibrationchain-qt6
+compasschain.depends = magcalibrationchain
